marta (devex): opened PR with a short migration + troubleshooting section for function/tool calling -> structured output. includes parse heuristics and a tiny shim for servers that want to accept both shapes. PTAL: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/623

owen (eng): Thanks. Two quick asks: 1) include a non-destructive repo replace example (perl -pi.bak) and a safer `git grep | xargs sed -n` suggestion; 2) show an explicit JS example that does `JSON.parse` in a try/catch — do not imply SDK auto-parses.

marta (devex): Yep will add both. PR currently has a perl backup line and a recommended grep+sed command. Also added a short changelog line to surface the shape standardization.

felix (ml): Please add a tiny normalization heuristic section (advanced) for the common issues we see: single quotes, trailing commas, stray newlines. Mark it advanced and warn it's lossy.

nora (docs): I drafted the JS/Python snippets and a minimal JSON Schema guardrail. Here's the JS snippet I plan to include (copy-friendly):
```js
const resp = await client.chat.complete(...);
const argsStr = resp.tool_call?.arguments ?? resp.tool?.args;
let args;
try {
  args = JSON.parse(argsStr);
} catch (err) {
  // fallback: keep raw value so callers can surface a helpful error
  args = { _raw: String(argsStr) };
}
// validate args with Ajv or similar before invoking tool
```

nora (docs): And Python: 
```python
resp = client.chat.complete(...)
args_raw = (resp.get('tool_call') or resp.get('tool') or {}).get('arguments')
try:
  args = json.loads(args_raw)
except Exception:
  args = {'_raw': str(args_raw)}
# validate args with jsonschema before use
```

felix (ml): For schema, suggest this compact anyOf variant to accept object-or-string (helps during rollout):
```json
{"type":"object","properties":{"tool_call":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string"},"arguments":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"object"}]}}},"required":["tool_call"]}
```

own (eng): Good. Also add unit-test suggestion: assert parser handles both `{"tool_call":{"name":"x","arguments":"{\"k\":1}"}}` and `{"tool_call":{"name":"x","arguments":{"k":1}}}` and a plain-text fallback.

marta (devex): Added tests suggestion and a short regression note in the PR description. I also included a tiny perl line: `perl -pi.bak -e 's/"tool"/"tool_call"/g' $(git grep -l '"tool"')` and a non-destructive jq transform for JSON fixtures.

